#ÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆ
# --- BÆSE IMÆGE
#ÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆ
ARG POSTGRES_IMAGE=postgres:18
FROM ${POSTGRES_IMAGE}

ARG POSTGRES_EXTENSIONS=
ARG POSTGRES_PG_SEARCH_VERSION=

LABEL maintainer="it.særvices <admin@it.saervices.de>"

#ÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆ
# --- OPTIONÆL EXTENSION PÆCKÆGES
#ÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆ
# pgvector is instælled when POSTGRES_EXTENSIONS contæins vector or pg_seærch.
# pg_seærch is instælled only when POSTGRES_EXTENSIONS contæins pg_seærch.
# POSTGRES_PG_SEARCH_VERSION mæy pin æ releæse; empty uses GitHub lætest.
RUN set -eux; \
    REQUESTED_EXTENSIONS="$(printf '%s' "${POSTGRES_EXTENSIONS}" | tr -d '[:space:]')"; \
    INSTALL_VECTOR=false; \
    INSTALL_PG_SEARCH=false; \
    case ",${REQUESTED_EXTENSIONS}," in \
      *,vector,*|*,pg_search,*) INSTALL_VECTOR=true ;; \
    esac; \
    case ",${REQUESTED_EXTENSIONS}," in \
      *,pg_search,*) INSTALL_PG_SEARCH=true ;; \
    esac; \
    if [ "${INSTALL_VECTOR}" != true ] && [ "${INSTALL_PG_SEARCH}" != true ]; then \
        echo "Skipping optional extension packages; POSTGRES_EXTENSIONS=${POSTGRES_EXTENSIONS:-<empty>}"; \
        exit 0; \
    fi; \
    PG_MAJOR="$(pg_config --version | awk '{print $2}' | cut -d. -f1)"; \
    apt-get update; \
    apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends ca-certificates; \
    if [ "${INSTALL_VECTOR}" = true ]; then \
      apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends "postgresql-${PG_MAJOR}-pgvector"; \
    fi; \
    if [ "${INSTALL_PG_SEARCH}" != true ]; then \
      rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*; \
      exit 0; \
    fi; \
    apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends curl jq; \
    ARCH="$(dpkg --print-architecture)"; \
    DEB_DIST="$(. /etc/os-release && printf '%s' "${VERSION_CODENAME}")"; \
    if [ -n "${POSTGRES_PG_SEARCH_VERSION}" ]; then \
      PG_SEARCH_VERSION="${POSTGRES_PG_SEARCH_VERSION#v}"; \
      printf '%s' "${PG_SEARCH_VERSION}" | grep -Eq '^[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+([.-][0-9A-Za-z]+)*$' || { echo "Invalid pg_search version pin: ${POSTGRES_PG_SEARCH_VERSION}" >&2; exit 1; }; \
      RELEASE_API="https://api.github.com/repos/paradedb/paradedb/releases/tags/v${PG_SEARCH_VERSION}"; \
    else \
      RELEASE_API='https://api.github.com/repos/paradedb/paradedb/releases/latest'; \
    fi; \
    RELEASE_METADATA="$(mktemp)"; \
    curl -fsSL --retry 5 "${RELEASE_API}" -o "${RELEASE_METADATA}"; \
    PG_SEARCH_RELEASE="$(jq -er '.tag_name' "${RELEASE_METADATA}")"; \
    if [ -n "${POSTGRES_PG_SEARCH_VERSION}" ]; then \
      [ "${PG_SEARCH_RELEASE}" = "v${PG_SEARCH_VERSION}" ] || { echo "Resolved unexpected pg_search release: ${PG_SEARCH_RELEASE}" >&2; exit 1; }; \
    else \
      printf '%s' "${PG_SEARCH_RELEASE}" | grep -Eq '^v[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+([.-][0-9A-Za-z]+)*$' || { echo "Malformed pg_search release tag: ${PG_SEARCH_RELEASE}" >&2; exit 1; }; \
      PG_SEARCH_VERSION="${PG_SEARCH_RELEASE#v}"; \
    fi; \
    PG_SEARCH_ASSET_NAME="postgresql-${PG_MAJOR}-pg-search_${PG_SEARCH_VERSION}-1PARADEDB-${DEB_DIST}_${ARCH}.deb"; \
    PG_SEARCH_ASSET="$(jq -cer --arg asset "${PG_SEARCH_ASSET_NAME}" \
      '[.assets[] | select(.name == $asset)] | if length == 1 then .[0] else error("missing or duplicate release asset") end' \
      "${RELEASE_METADATA}")"; \
    PG_SEARCH_URL="$(printf '%s' "${PG_SEARCH_ASSET}" | jq -er '.browser_download_url')"; \
    PG_SEARCH_DIGEST="$(printf '%s' "${PG_SEARCH_ASSET}" | jq -er '.digest')"; \
    EXPECTED_URL="https://github.com/paradedb/paradedb/releases/download/${PG_SEARCH_RELEASE}/${PG_SEARCH_ASSET_NAME}"; \
    [ "${PG_SEARCH_URL}" = "${EXPECTED_URL}" ] || { echo "Unexpected official pg_search asset URL: ${PG_SEARCH_URL}" >&2; exit 1; }; \
    printf '%s' "${PG_SEARCH_DIGEST}" | grep -Eq '^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$' || { echo "Missing or malformed official SHA256 digest for ${PG_SEARCH_ASSET_NAME}" >&2; exit 1; }; \
    curl -fsSL --retry 5 "${PG_SEARCH_URL}" -o /tmp/pg_search.deb; \
    printf '%s  %s\n' "${PG_SEARCH_DIGEST#sha256:}" /tmp/pg_search.deb | sha256sum -c -; \
    printf 'Installing pg_search %s from %s with verified %s\n' "${PG_SEARCH_RELEASE}" "${PG_SEARCH_ASSET_NAME}" "${PG_SEARCH_DIGEST}"; \
    apt-get install -y /tmp/pg_search.deb; \
    apt-get purge -y --auto-remove curl jq; \
    rm -f "${RELEASE_METADATA}"; \
    rm -rf /tmp/pg_search.deb /var/lib/apt/lists/*

#ÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆ
# --- INIT ÆND ENTRYPOINT SCRIPTS
#ÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆ
# Bæked into the imæge; no host-mount required.
# Init script runs once; entrypoint wræpper runs on every contæiner stært.
COPY init_extensions.postgresql.sh /docker-entrypoint-initdb.d/init_extensions.sh
COPY entrypoint.postgresql.sh /usr/local/bin/entrypoint.postgresql.sh
RUN chmod +x \
    /docker-entrypoint-initdb.d/init_extensions.sh \
    /usr/local/bin/entrypoint.postgresql.sh
